      "content": "the thing is, there actually isn't a \"Risk Exposure Matrix\" or a \"Future Outlook\" section in the report they just sent over. it's a pretty standard, straightforward summary of the tests we ran. if i point them to sections that don't exist, it's going to be pretty obvious i'm making stuff up. \n\nis there a way to sell this package without having to invent actual parts of the report? like, can we just frame the current security as \"stagnant\" or something without actually lying about what's written in the document?",
